torrent represents the most important  feature of eldon ring the open world he  is our gateway to explore the vast world  through but unfortunately he falls flat  from a gameplay perspective  everyone mad luigi here in this video i  want to take a slightly different style  than many of my previous videos because  i want to talk about some aspects of  elden ring beyond just the lore i want  to talk about the gameplay around  torrent and my issues with it  if you saw my torrent lore video you  will have some idea what i mean as a  character torrent has some backstory and  motivational development but he seems  not fully realized for what he is our  constant companion who is with us  throughout the game and this feeling of  incompleteness only grows when we  consider the core experience of the game  which is the gameplay when you start the  game you are quickly given torrent to  assist in your open world exploration he  makes for a companion who is always with  you and opens up a new way to quickly  traverse the world whether that be  through galloping around or jumping up  onto things with your double jump and he  also allows for mounted combat which  often gives you an edge over foot  soldiers grounded enemies and even  flying enemies but as you progress  through the game leveling up increasing  your stats and gaining new abilities  torrance stays almost exactly the same  throughout the entire game  your experience at level 1 on torrent is  going to be nearly identical to your  experience at level 100 the only  ostensible changes are maybe a health  increase and the fact that leveling  dexterity is supposed to make it harder  to get knocked off of torrent but it  very much didn't feel this way in my  playthrough and when i went to test it i  couldn't find any evidence to support  either of these ideas the health on  torrent seems unchanged by whether or  not i'm on a late game level 100 plus  character or on a brand new level 10  character and the ability to be knocked  off torrent seems the same regardless of  level i tested on a character with  literally level 1 decks and a character  with max 99 decks and it took the same  number of enemy attacks to unseat me  from torrent a basic limb grave enemy  with a torch took me off torrent in five  hits in both cases and a kite and  sellsword took me off torn on both  characters and three to four swings of  his sort  maybe something in these tests missed  how torn's poise is supposed to work but  in my time with the game it has felt  like there isn't really any change to  torrent despite how much i progressed my  character i never felt like i could take  more hits from even basic early game  enemies before torrent would disappear  and i'd be locked into a falling  animation  and this lack of progression is my core  issue with torrent especially because  there are so so so many ways to make  torrent feel like part of our journey of  progression ways which would fit because  torrent is supposed to be somewhat of a  character  the first potential changes are obvious  and connected with what we just  discussed make tangible upgrades to  torrance health stamina and poi is  possible these can either scale directly  with the player like how it is supposed  to do with decks or be tied to items or  armor found throughout the world giving  players the opportunity to increase  tauren's health and stamina can make it  feel like he is growing to meet new  challenges just like us the player  increasing poise and the ability to  withstand more hits would help to show  progression and give a feeling to the  player of really having grown and being  stronger when returning to earlier areas  a similar upgrade that would help  torrent be more fun would be the  possibility of increasing his speed  maybe i'm a bit biased because i always  love speed increases in games like how  crackdown 2's agility orbs are some of  my favorite experiences in gaming but  some speed upgrades for torrent  throughout the game could work well to  make traversing the large sections of  the map more enjoyable these could be  more restrictive than the other upgrades  as speed is a pretty sensitive thing to  the rhythm of fromsoft games and they  could even be disabled for the few boss  fights that allow torrent in them but  getting to return to lyrnia or caled as  a late game character and gallop through  them at a couple tiers of faster speed  would be a great feeling  and as torrent is a spectral steed these  could be accompanied by some added  spirit effects to denote the higher  speeds maybe they could be tiers of  speed that can be unlocked and activated  for a certain maybe limited amount of  time so you're not always zooming around  at 200 speed but you still get to  traverse the large open world a bit  faster and slotting these upgrades  towards the late game would allow the  balance present in most of the game to  stay the same for your first playthrough  and an associated quality of life change  would be to make the galloping a bit  more streamlined so the player doesn't  have to repeatedly spam the run button  to make torrent maintain full speed and  in line with this kind of spirit speed  upgrade i think another really obvious  area for more progression for torrent  can be found in the ancestral spirits  if you saw my lore video you might be  able to guess it but i think allowing  torrent to unlock a third jump like the  regal ancestor has would be a classic  video game upgrade if we also want to  let torrent into these fights which  would fit since they have such big  arenas and given the lore connection  between tauren and the spirits we could  have tauren unlock the third jump after  defeating one of them and then use it  during the fight with the second one  which would be very thematic or just  unlocking it after the second one works  too and it would also be cool to be able  to attack when torrent makes his second  jump or in this case even his third  now this is going to be one of the  biggest reaches of a change despite how  straightforward it seems because a third  jump would let the player access more  things vertically so the world would  have had to been designed with that in  mind because that would be a lot of work  this is less plausible as a change that  could be implemented now it would have  had to be considered when the game world  was being created but it still seems  like something that could have fit in  really well making it a mid to late game  unlock that lets us access new heights  and areas  and a note on bosses too it would have  been great to see torrent especially a  torrent with more upgrades in more boss  fights ranala has a very open second  phase to allow for torrent just make her  float around a bit more spoiler warning  and of course the elden beast fight  would have been a fantastic opportunity  for torrance inclusion both thematically  and gameplay-wise he is our constant  companion around since the start of the  game so having him there at the end of  the game would be great and him being  around for the gameplay would limit the  time spent chasing the elden beast and  make for a very cinematic final fight  which is obviously what from software is  going for in theme  to cap off the ability discussion we  can't use ashes of war while on torrent  so why not allow us to unlock combat  abilities to be used instead a great  candidate would be the body slam attack  that many of the horse-based bosses use  against us like the knight's cavalry and  the tree sentinels body slams stomps or  other combat options would give more  variety to mounted gameplay and allow  for some cool new unlocks from horse  bosses how cool would it be to defeat a  knight's cavalry and instead of getting  a random ash of war you get one of their  horse's attacks  and we will have truly come full circle  with the next suggestion but it needs to  be said  horse armor in a similar way to player  armor horse armor could provide  aesthetic variety to torrent signify and  reward player exploration and even allow  players to modify torrent to their given  playstyle  heavy armor could make torrents slow but  sturdier able to withstand more attacks  before disappearing light armor can make  torrent lighter and more stamina  friendly while sacrificing defense and  poise we've come a long way since the  original horse armor dlc fiasco but i  think this would be a worthwhile change  that could fit with the themes of the  game in progression rpg playstyle  variants and exploration  all of these upgrades and abilities and  armor possibilities would also really  help with one of the other main issues i  have with the game the loot because the  open world of eldon ring is so big it  can sometimes feel less worthwhile to  explore when a lot of the loot you find  ends up being extremely class dependent  or unusable to your playstyle or  roleplay this is something joseph  anderson mentioned in his critique video  that resonated with me these torn  upgrades would give a chance to include  more universal loot in a lot of the  areas of the game so players could still  find their desired spells and other  items but they'd also be unlocking more  universal upgrades more people would  have more reason and reward to do more  exploration it would also make the  repetitive caves and catacombs a little  bit more bearable if you were more  confident that they would surely give  you something that would benefit your  playthrough and this would carry over to  subsequent playthroughs too making them  more enticing to do more exploration  there are more possibilities i could  discuss like the ability to interact  with torrent outside of mounted gameplay  such as to pet him or to have some form  of character development with him as his  lore suggests should be there to some  degree there are small things like the  annoying message asking if you want to  revive him every time he dies or how the  player dying doesn't reset torrent's  health but i think enough examples have  been given to illustrate the point oh  except for one last one which would be  really easy to implement more  consumables with all the ingredients and  crafting in the game or that the game  wants us to do we could be able to make  different berry mixtures or flavored  raisins that affect torrent either  making him faster granting him certain  abilities offering buffs or any other  kind of possible effect this would also  be more feasible to implement in an  update or offer in dlc  torrent is a defining feature of nunes  and eldon ring he is essentially the  conduit of the open world and next to  nothing is done with him he gets  essentially no progression in gameplay  or in lore character or story he could  have been one more grand avenue for  fromsoft to drive home the benefits of  exploration and increase the fun of open  world traversal  instead he is utterly static and doesn't  contribute anything more to the game in  the middle or end than he does the  moment you receive him in a game that is  so clearly focused on exploration and  rpg progression he stands out as a  lacking area which doesn't flow with so  many of eldon rings core themes  i think torrent is a great addition but  because he could have been so much more  i think he clearly stands as one of the  game's biggest letdowns and missed  opportunities not as something  necessarily bad but as something that  could have made this already wonderful  game even that much better  and that is the summary of my feelings  on torrent as a gameplay mechanic i hope  you enjoyed the video even if you're  someone who comes to my channel for lore  torrent is a good case where the lore  and gameplay share similar themes of  comment and how they both could have  been expanded so i thought this was a  good place to bridge into a gameplay  discussion if you want more elder ring  videos make sure you subscribe since  i'll be making more lore videos and more  videos like this where i discuss  features of the game beyond just the  lore i think i even want to do a full  game critique soon so this is like stage  1 of that well thank you all for  watching and i'll see you in the next  video bye

